{"item_id": "dbe-mathematics-g10-p1-2018-nov-5.1.1", "source_id": "dbe-mathematics-g10-p1-2018-nov", "pair_source_id": "dbe-mathematics-g10-p1-2018-nov-memo", "subject": "mathematics", "grade": 12, "language": "en", "track": "core_maths", "kind": "question", "question_ref": "5.1.1", "marks": 2, "topic": "Functions: Quadratic and Exponential", "passage": "Sketched below are the graphs of $f(x) = ax^2 + q$ and $g(x) = \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^x - 4$. A and B are the $x$-intercepts of $f$. The graphs intersect at A and point $E(1 ; 3)$ lies on $f$. C is the turning point of $f$ and D is the $y$-intercept of $g$.", "question": "Write down the coordinates of D.", "memo": "D is the y-intercept of g: g(0) = (1/2)^0 - 4 = 1 - 4 = -3. $\\checkmark$ Coordinates: (0; -3) $\\checkmark$", "final_answer": "(0; -3)", "needs_review": false, "licence": "DBE copyright - check terms", "attribution": "Department of Basic Education"}
